From: Daniel Vicory <dvicory@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Jul 2026 02:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(terminal): add Gondolin broker terminal backend

Add a BaseEnvironment implementation that routes terminal execution
through the profile's Gondolin broker over its mode-0600 Unix socket
(HERMES_GONDOLIN_SOCKET). The backend is a thin typed client of the
broker protocol: ensure on construction (surfacing recreation as
trusted state-loss context), exec.start for commands with streamed
bounded output and exec.cancel on kill, and close on cleanup. The
broker owns images, policy, lifecycle, network mediation, and resource
governance; the gateway never selects them.

Registers env_type "gondolin" in the environment factory, the container
cwd guard, the unknown-backend error, and the tool health check (broker
status probe). File tools use the generic ShellFileOperations path;
background processes and execute_code ride the shared env contract.
Kept as a separate patch from conversation identity and worker-lane
changes so each is independently reviewable (V3 section 14.4).

